WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.687
The phrase candidate clean row is intentional.

00:00:02.687 --> 00:00:06.517
Passing selected checks does not mean every fact is verified.

00:00:06.517 --> 00:00:10.527
It means the row satisfies the rules we implemented for this exercise.

00:00:10.527 --> 00:00:12.647
Review rows still need attention.

00:00:12.647 --> 00:00:16.057
Duplicate ranking still requires policy or evidence.

00:00:16.057 --> 00:00:19.747
Use labels that accurately describe what your process knows.

00:00:19.747 --> 00:00:24.462
Connect this idea to a customer master-data project cleaning duplicate profiles.

00:00:24.462 --> 00:00:29.297
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:29.297 --> 00:00:35.897
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:35.897 --> 00:00:40.687
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:40.687 --> 00:00:45.680
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
